data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":1574,"item_id":"fc_0bc21c3f5cc2a75d016adb4fe906948191869325e1db7cffa2","output_index":2,"arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"inference\":\"R001\",\"packet_sha256\":\"861560366e50e9871f53ed492d9eb069b7f844d36c01073c478b84be1047e7fd\",\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Packet-only mathematical review: the first unsupported implication is in S001. N002 does not state differentiability of E or a formula for E′; it only repeats integrability and compact-support/continuity facts. The claimed differentiability and derivative formula are therefore unavailable. This blocks the conclusion, regardless of the later N003–N004 argument. Inputs are treated as allowed conditional premises; no source-fidelity judgment is made. I read this packet and the declared Audit A, self-containment, and format rules in this context. I cannot attest a separate fresh carrier/context or runtime isolation; packet_replay is UNVERIFIED. Carrier identity, canonical hash binding, and transmitted-material readback are outside this mathematical review.\",\"checks\":{\"inputs\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The argument's cited N and M proposition statements are present in this packet and, as directed, are treated as conditional premises. The explicitly shown r is positive and the stated M015 instantiation is compatible with its stated zero-integral result. This does not validate source fidelity.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/0/statement\",\"/inputs/1/statement\",\"/inputs/2/statement\",\"/inputs/3/statement\",\"/inputs/4/source_contract\"]},\"argument\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"First unsupported step: S001 says N002 states differentiability of E at r and E′(r)=∫e_t(x,r)dx. The actual N002 statement contains no differentiability assertion or derivative identity. Nothing in the argument proves these. Thus S001's claimed derivative fact is unsupported, and the target cannot be concluded. S002's zero-integrand reasoning does not establish the missing differentiability/derivative formula.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inputs/1/statement\",\"/output/statement\"]},\"dependency_accounting\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The factual use attributed to N002 in S001 (differentiability and the derivative formula) is not among N002's contents; this is an ungrounded factual claim, not merely an accounting omission. Other inputs have identifiable intended roles, including N001/N002 for integrability, N003 for the energy derivative expression, N004 for pointwise vanishing, and M015 for the zero integral.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/0/uses\",\"/inputs/1/statement\"]},\"output\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The output requires differentiability of E at every r>0 and E′(r)=0. The inference does not establish differentiability or the derivative expression it attributes to N002. The output is therefore not derived, although the integrability clause is present in N001 (and repeated in N002).\",\"locations\":[\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inputs/1/statement\"]},\"scope\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The proof fixes arbitrary positive r and claims the clauses for that r; the arbitrary variable's recorded scope covers both argument steps. No temporary assumptions or witnesses are introduced or escape scope. This scope judgment does not cure the missing premise.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/locals/0\",\"/inference/argument/0\",\"/inference/argument/1\"]},\"applicability\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"For the mathematical conditional review of the packet's stated M015 contract, the proposed binding X=ℝⁿ, μ=Lebesgue measure, V=ℝ and the identically zero integrand from N004 fit the stated zero-integral result; the packet supplies the Borel/Lebesgue and real-space conditions. This establishes only that subapplication, not the missing N002 claim. Actual library source/signature fidelity is separate and not verified here.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/4/source_contract\",\"/inputs/3/statement\",\"/inference/applications/0\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\"]},\"statement_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The input and output prose supplies the formulas and conditions relevant to this R without requiring a producer proof. In particular, N002's actual full content is clear and does not contain the derivative assertion made in S001. Treating this check as closed does not mean the inference follows.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/0/statement\",\"/inputs/1/statement\",\"/inputs/2/statement\",\"/inputs/3/statement\",\"/inputs/4/statement\",\"/output/statement\"]},\"object_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"S002 uses h as an integrand abbreviation, explicitly defining it inline, but h is absent from the local declaration inventory. The text makes its intended meaning recoverable, but the packet's object inventory/scope record does not register this actual mathematical object. Other named primary objects (r, u, E, n, Δ_x and the M015 instantiation) have declarations in the packet.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/locals\",\"/inputs/2/statement\",\"/inputs/3/statement\"]},\"dependency_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Actual prose uses N002 as grounds for differentiability and E′=∫e_t, which that input does not assert and which is not derived locally. This is the first dependency-closure defect. The later pointwise-zero and zero-integral claims have direct stated grounds, but cannot repair that defect.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/0/uses\",\"/inputs/1/statement\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\"]},\"packet_replay\":{\"verdict\":\"UNVERIFIED\",\"notes\":\"The mathematical review in this context used the complete frozen packet and relevant declared Yui rules, with no other mathematical task material. I cannot represent this context as a separate fresh carrier, attest isolation/runtime execution, or provide a fresh-carrier execution record. Per the replay standard, a fresh replay therefore remains UNVERIFIED. Input boundary: packet.json plus the read Audit A/self-containment/format rules; no source proofs or other R bodies.\",\"locations\":[\"/warning\",\"/packet_sha256\"]}},\"findings\":[{\"location\":\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"premises\":\"N002's actual statement: integrability and interval/compact-set, continuity and vanishing conditions.\",\"conclusion_claimed\":\"E is differentiable at r and E′(r)=∫e_t(x,r)dx.\",\"judgment\":\"Unsupported; N002 says neither, and no local proof supplies either fact. This is the first unsupported implication and blocks the target.\"},{\"location\":\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"premises\":\"N004 states pointwise vanishing of the displayed product; M015 states that an identically zero function has zero integral, subject to its stated space conditions.\",\"conclusion_claimed\":\"The whole-space integral in N003 is zero.\",\"judgment\":\"Conditionally supported by the packet's stated premises and M015 contract, but it does not establish the missing differentiability/derivative formula.\"},{\"location\":\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"premises\":\"Inline abbreviation h(x)=... in S002.\",\"conclusion_claimed\":\"h is an available integrand object.\",\"judgment\":\"Its meaning is given inline, but it is omitted from the inference local-object inventory; object closure fails.\"}]}}"}

